  "notes": "This leaf continues scan 004’s “peut-on le” with “factoriser canoniquement en”, yielding the canonical factorization (10). The author asks whether the ambiguity of a deck transformation disappears in the isotopy category, expressed by (11). He reduces to f₀=id and to finite-order surface automorphisms isotopic to the identity. The final sentence continues on scan 005, which is physically earlier in the supplied order. The consolidated file keeps scan order.\n\nThe author’s own question marks are preserved after the isotopy description and (11). In (11), cancellation of an invertible f₀ in the isotopy category reduces γf₀~f₀ to γ~id; the assertion γ=id remains precisely the question, not a formal consequence. The subsequent free-action assertion is carried as the author’s claim, without silently adding connectedness or faithfulness assumptions. The odd wording “une d’exigence” remains. Pencil page 5; no manuscript page number or date.",
